      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "To start the process"
      ],
      "justification": "Initiates the process as described in the opening phrase. The action node faithfully restates the starting point."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n2"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Course Packet Information Received should be sent"
      ],
      "justification": "Direct match for the first required messaging action."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n3"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "followed by sending the Design to Faculty"
      ],
      "justification": "Direct match for the second sequential messaging action."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n5"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After sending the Design to Faculty, the Faculty will choose the design."
      ],
      "justification": "Captures the faculty selection step immediately following the design submission."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n4"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Next, identify the content that requires copyright clearance and contact the publisher to obtain clearance."
      ],
      "justification": "Matches the clearance identification and publisher contact step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "label:n4->b1",
        "guard:b1->n6",
        "action:n6"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If there is a need to \"Contact Faculty to inform of denial and ask if new content should be added\", then the process should be continued."
      ],
      "justification": "Models the denial/continuation branch. The converge node structurally handles the loop-back implied by 'process should be continued'. Guards and labels correctly split and route the flow based on the stated condition."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b1->n7",
        "action:n7"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if the \"Entire Course Packet Copyright Cleared\", then the MPC should Calculate the Course Packet Cost."
      ],
      "justification": "Models the alternative cleared/calculation branch correctly."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n8"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After calculating the Course Packet Cost, the MPC should add the Bookstore margin to determine the retail price."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct match for the margin addition and pricing step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "label:n8->b2",
        "guard:b2->n12",
        "action:n12"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the Faculty needs to reconsider the course packet content to decrease the price, then the process should be continued."
      ],
      "justification": "Models the reconsideration/continuation branch. The branch structure and guard correctly capture the conditional loop-back described in the source."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b2->n10",
        "action:n10"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Alternatively, if the Price of the Course Packet is finalized, then the MPC should notify the Bookstore of the Course packet, Course number, Faculty name, and sections."
      ],
      "justification": "Models the finalization/notification branch correctly. Content matches the specified details to be communicated."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n11"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once the MPC notifies the Bookstore, the Packet information should be notified to the Bookstore, and the process will end."
      ],
      "justification": "Matches the final notification step and explicitly terminates the process as stated."
    }
  ],
